r after the first day of the Late Stage Indicator.","How to read the table: every heading sorts the table. Green = the test is met; amber = partly met or close; red = the wrong side of the test. Depth of a fall from the six-month high: Shallow Pullback 10% to 15%, Medium Pullback 15% to 20%, Deep Pullback over 20%. A date reads \"Fri 13-Nov (4D)\": the day, then how many days ago it was."],"early":["What this page lists: every stock the signed rules classify today, as new capital, as Broadening / Early S2 Core Investment: Stage 2 (advancing) rated Probable or Plausible, with no completed pullback or base yet since Stage 2 (advancing) began (it is in its first, or has not had one).","One route. Add on Healthy Retest: Pulling Back? (Early Stage Indicator), then a 1st Retest of a rising moving average on low volume (Late Stage Indicator), then a trigger day closing above that moving average. The Retest columns show which moving average is being retested, how far the price is from it, how long the Retest has run and its volume.","Before tranche 1: Market Cycle Phase Uptrend. The four VCP tests are shown for information: a VCP breakout is not an entry route for this classification in the signed rules.","A trigger day: the share price up 1.5% or more on the day, volume 1.20 times its 50-day average or more, and the close in the top quarter of the day's range. It counts only on or after the first day of the Late Stage Indicator.","How to read the table: every heading sorts the table. Green = the test is met; amber = partly met or close; red = the wrong side of the test. Depth of a fall from the six-month high: Shallow Pullback 10% to 15%, Medium Pullback 15% to 20%, Deep Pullback over 20%. A date reads \"Fri 13-Nov (4D)\": the day, then how many days ago it was."],"inflecting":["What this page lists: every stock the signed rules classify today, as new capital, as Inflecting / S1→S2 Probing Bet: turning from Stage 1 (bottoming) to Stage 2 (advancing). A stock is here when its 150-day moving average crossed above its 200-day, or its 200-day turned up, in the last week, or when either is expected within the next month at the last 10 sessions' rate.","Four separate routes. ONE route is enough: each route has its own Early Stage Indicator and Late Stage Indicator, and a stock's furthest step is the furthest it has reached on any one route. The cross and the turn-up are not both needed. The route is named under the furthest step.","Route 1, the 150-day crossing above the 200-day. Early Stage Indicator, Crossing Soon?: the cross is expected within 21 sessions at the last 10 sessions' rate. Late Stage Indicator, Crossed?: it crossed in the last week, with up-day volume over the last 5 sessions at 1.20 times the 50-day average or more.","Route 2, the 200-day turning up. Early Stage Indicator, Turning Up Soon?: the 200-day is expected to stand higher than 21 sessions earlier within 21 sessions. Late Stage Indicator, Turned Up?: it did so in the last week, with the same up-day volume.","Routes 3 and 4, the 5-day and the 10-day turning up. Early Stage Indicator, Flattening?: the line fell over the last week and its fall has slowed by two-thirds or stopped. Late Stage Indicator, Turned Up?: the line rose on each of the last two sessions, having fallen earlier in the week, and has not fallen since.","A trigger day: the share price up 1.5% or more on the day, volume 1.20 times its 50-day average or more, and the close in the top quarter of the day's range. It counts only on or after the first day of the Late Stage Indicator.","How to read the table: every heading sorts the table. Green = the test is met; amber = partly met or close; red = the wrong side of the test. Depth of a fall from the six-month high: Shallow Pullback 10% to 15%, Medium Pullback 15% to 20%, Deep Pullback over 20%. A date reads \"Fri 13-Nov (4D)\": the day, then how many days ago it was."],"s1":["What this page lists: every stock the signed rules classify today, as new capital,